   "text": "Reading the ring clockwise from the top, I identified these residues:\n\n- Asp, with its \u03b1-carboxyl as a piperidine amide and its side-chain carbonyl joined to the next ring nitrogen.\n- Pipecolic acid.\n- Phe.\n- N-Me-Leu.\n- Leu.\n- N-Me-Ile.\n- Gly.\n- N-Me-Leu.\n- Thr.\n- Pro.\n- Phe, which closes back onto the Asp NH.\n\nThe short link between the top \u03b1-carbon and the carbonyl beside the pipecolic nitrogen looked slightly long, so I read it as a CH2. That makes the first residue Asp rather than an aminomalonyl unit.\n\nFor stereochemistry I applied the CORN rule to each wedge or hash in the drawing. Every \u03b1-carbon came out as the L configuration, and the Ile \u03b2-carbon is S and the Thr \u03b2-carbon is R, as in the natural amino acids. I then wrote the SMILES with the matching chirality tags.\n\nSMILES: [C@@H]1(C(=O)N2CCCCC2)CC(=O)N3CCCC[C@H]3C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc4ccccc4)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)NCC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N5CCC[C@H]5C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc6ccccc6)C(=O)N1"
